module_specs:
  pixel_clock: |
    Use an MMCM to derive the 74.25 MHz pixel clock from the 100 MHz board oscillator:
    DIVCLK_DIVIDE=5, CLKFBOUT_MULT_F=37.125, and CLKOUT0_DIVIDE_F=10.
    Expose the MMCM lock indication for clock-stability blanking and the LED.
  timing_gen: |
    Generate a continuous 1650-by-750 raster at 74.25 MHz. Mark the 1280-by-720 active
    region and generate positive horizontal and vertical sync using the specified porches.
    Increment the 32-bit unsigned frame counter once per completed frame; it wraps naturally.
    Assert frame_start on the first raster sample of each frame.
  pattern_gen: |
    On active coordinates, generate eight 160-pixel vertical bars in the order white,
    yellow, cyan, green, magenta, red, blue, black by default. Pattern select 0 selects
    bars; pattern select 1 selects solid black. Preserve raster metadata and frame_start.
  median_filter: |
    For each active output coordinate, calculate the median independently for each
    4-bit colour channel over its 3x3 neighbourhood. At picture boundaries, clamp
    neighbourhood coordinates to the nearest active-picture coordinate. Preserve the
    corresponding coordinate, active-video indication, sync timing, and frame_start.
  vga_output: |
    Drive 4-bit RGB and positive-polarity sync outputs from the filtered raster. Drive
    RGB to zero outside active video, while BTNC is pressed, while the pixel clock is
    not locked, and during reset. Consume the stream without backpressure.

requirements:
  - id: S-1
    text: "Generate VGA timing at 1280x720 and 60 Hz using a 74.25 MHz pixel clock, 1650 clocks per line (1280 active, 110 front porch, 40 sync, 220 back porch), and 750 lines per frame (720 active, 5 front porch, 5 sync, 20 back porch), with positive horizontal and vertical sync."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [pixel_clock, timing_gen, vga_output, top]
  - id: S-2
    text: "By default, generate eight vertical bars, each 160 pixels wide, in this order: white, yellow, cyan, green, magenta, red, blue, black."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [pattern_gen, top]
  - id: S-3
    text: "For pixels with a complete 3x3 neighbourhood, output the median of the nine neighbourhood values independently for each colour channel."
    proof: [simulation, formal]
    modules: [median_filter, top]
  - id: S-4
    text: "Keep the output picture, active-video indication, and horizontal and vertical sync aligned so that each output picture coordinate corresponds to the sync and active-video timing for that coordinate."
    proof: [simulation, formal]
    modules: [timing_gen, pattern_gen, median_filter, vga_output, top]
  - id: S-5
    text: "Drive all colour outputs to zero outside the active picture, while BTNC is pressed, and while the pixel clock is not stable."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [vga_output, top]
  - id: S-6
    text: "Illuminate LED[0] when the pixel clock is stable."
    proof: [hardware]
    modules: [pixel_clock, top]
  - id: S-7
    text: "Provide a USB-UART test shell at 115200 baud that identifies the design as VMED."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [top]
  - id: S-8
    text: "Through the USB-UART test shell, allow the host to select a test pattern and read a frame counter."
    proof: [simulation, hardware]
    modules: [pattern_gen, timing_gen, top]

